1612	
1613	Every family filters observations at delivery. A resumed iterator with only POST_ORDER selected suppresses a buffered PRE_ORDER event; an event committed while emission was disabled can still be selected if it has not yet reached delivery. Deferred DAG settlement records its committed work observation independently of the selector used to admit the work. Filtering never repeats callbacks, resolutions or committed W/C transitions. Once an observation has been delivered or suppressed at delivery, it is consumed and cannot be recovered by changing the selector.
1614	
1615	Explicit required `emitEvents` arrays narrow iterator results to their selected kinds/phases on concrete runners and execution capabilities; an empty array yields `never`. No argument, an undefined selector or options with an optional selector retain the broad event type because the persisted policy is unknown. Heterogeneous unions can also retain broad inference; preserve the family capability when wrapping a runner. `SelectedTraversalEvent<Event, Kind>` describes the selected public record while retaining its data, ID and observation facets. There is no timing-policy option.
1616	
1617	Root flags describe family-specific boundaries. Tree `isTreeRoot` and DAG `isGraphRoot` identify the resolved container root. There is no separate traversal-start predicate or subtree-start option. Synthetic graph holders are bookkeeping and hidden from public events, views, and source-context parent fields. Walking uses `via: null` for an entry occurrence; under route policies, the same ID reached through a link has a non-null `via`. These meanings do not imply a shared root flag.
1618	
1619	The six tree/DAG runners use the same explicit transition-state model. Synchronous runners execute its callback requests inline; asynchronous runners delegate iteration and `run()` to one shared internal async session with serialized state commits, finite callback limiting when configured, and one iterator lease. Calling `run()` while an iterator owns that session rejects rather than starting a second execution.
1620	
1621	For reusable wrappers, use `TraversalExecutionState` (`getStatus`, `getStopReason`, `isHalted`, `inspect`, `requestPause`), `SyncTraversalExecution<Phase, Event>`, or `AsyncTraversalExecution<Phase, Event>`. Run returns this / Promise of this; iterators are closeable `Generator<Event, void, unknown>` / `AsyncGenerator<Event, void, unknown>`. Preserve the family's phase enum: a DFS abstraction rejects DAG phases and cannot widen to accept them. The emitted-kind default is `EmissionKind<Phase>`: DAG emission accepts committed `workCompleted`/`subgraphCompleted` names, and visitor selection accepts `ON_WORK_READY`/`ON_SUBGRAPH_READY`.
